tion_status\": \"parameter_mismatch\"\n}\n\n\n--- run_trace/galaxy_tool_run_002/validation_response.json\n{\n  \"action\": \"/tool_runner/index\",\n  \"citations\": true,\n  \"creator\": null,\n  \"credentials\": [],\n  \"description\": \"tree and alignment metrics for single files or collections\",\n  \"display\": true,\n  \"edam_operations\": [],\n  \"edam_topics\": [],\n  \"enctype\": \"application/x-www-form-urlencoded\",\n  \"errors\": {},\n  \"form_style\": \"regular\",\n  \"has_parameters\": true,\n  \"help\": \"<p>This wrapper exposes selected PhyKIT tree and alignment metrics.</p>\\n<div class=\\\"section\\\" id=\\\"input-modes\\\">\\n<h1>Input modes</h1>\\n<p>Single-file mode preserves the direct PhyKIT output for one tree or alignment.\\nCollection mode runs the selected metric for each member of one Galaxy\\ncollection and writes a combined table. Grouped-collection mode accepts repeated\\ngroup labels plus collections and writes a long table suitable for downstream\\ngroup comparison tools.</p>\\n<p>ZIP archive modes are convenience inputs for archive-heavy histories. They\\nextract local Galaxy ZIP datasets inside the job working directory, reject unsafe\\nmember paths such as absolute paths or <tt class=\\\"docutils literal\\\">..</tt> traversal, apply the same\\nsuffix/regular-expression filters, and then run the selected PhyKIT metric.\\nGalaxy-native collection mode remains the preferred route when users want to\\ninspect or reuse extracted archive members.</p>\\n<p>Collection outputs include:</p>\\n<ul class=\\\"simple\\\">\\n<li>a metrics table with group, file identifier, file name, metric, value, and\\nstatus columns;</li>\\n<li>a failed-files table with nonzero or unparsable PhyKIT runs; and</li>\\n<li>a summary table with total, selected, processed, failed, and skipped file\\ncounts per group.</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p>Use suffix or regular-expression filters when a collection contains mixed files,\\nfor example to process only <tt class=\\\"docutils literal\\\">.treefile</tt> members for tree metrics. In ZIP\\nmodes, leaving both filters blank processes every regular archive member and\\nwrites a warning to standard error.</p>\\n</div>\\n\",\n  \"help_format\": \"restructuredtext\",\n  \"hidden\": \"\",\n  \"hidden_versions\": [],\n  \"history_id\": \"bbd44e69cb8906b5f8d5e06ef09f4395\",\n  \"icon\": null,\n  \"id\": \"toolshed.g2.bx.psu.edu/repos/goeckslab/phykit_metrics/phykit_metrics/0.2.0+galaxy0\",\n  \"inputs\": [\n    {\n      \"cases\": [\n        {\n          \"inputs\": [\n            {\n              \"cases\": [\n                {\n                  \"inputs\": [\n                    {\n                      \"argument\": null,\n                      \"default_value\": {\n                        \"values\": [\n                          {\n                            \"id\": \"f9cad7b01a4721352099cf9f5a1ace62\",\n                            \"src\": \"hda\"\n                          }\n                        ]\n                      },\n                      \"edam\": {\n                        \"edam_data\": [\n                          \"data_0872\",\n                          \"data_0006\"\n                        ],\n                        \"edam_formats\": [\n                          \"format_1910\",\n                          \"format_2330\"\n                        ]\n                      },\n                      \"extensions\": [\n                        \"newick\",\n                        \"txt\"\n                      ],\n                      \"help\": \"\",\n                      \"help_format\": \"html\",\n                      \"hidden\": false,\n                      \"is_dynamic\": false,\n                      \"label\": \"tree file\",\n                      \"model_class\": \"DataToolParameter\",\n                      \"multiple\": false,\n                      \"name\": \"input\",\n                      \"optional\": false,\n                      \"options\": {\n           